A thin horizontal or vertical line that separates content.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/separator)

<%= embed UI::SeparatorPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Separator()
Separator(orientation: :vertical)
Separator(variant: :wave, class: "text-primary my-4")
```

Horizontal by default - a full-width rule - and a vertical divider with `orientation: :vertical`, stretching to the
height of its flex row. The line is drawn with `currentColor` (`text-border` by default), so any `text-*` class recolors it.

## Examples

### Variants

`solid`, `dashed`, `double` and `gradient` are CSS; `dotted`, `wave` and `zigzag` are a repeating SVG pattern that
scales with the available width.

