## API reference

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `orientation:` | `:horizontal`, `:vertical` | `:horizontal` | Direction of the line; vertical stretches to its flex parent. |
| `variant:` | `:solid`, `:dashed`, `:dotted`, `:double`, `:gradient`, `:wave`, `:zigzag` | `:solid` | Line style. |
| `class:` | `String` | - | Extra classes, merged via tailwind_merge. Set `text-*` to recolor, `my-*` / `mx-*` for spacing. |

The line weight follows the theme's `--border-width` (1px). Exposes `data-orientation` and `data-variant`.

## Accessibility

- Renders `role="separator"` with `aria-orientation`, so assistive tech announces the boundary.
- The default `text-border` is intentionally low-emphasis - use `text-border-strong` / `-intense` where it must stay visible.
- A separator is not interactive and is skipped by keyboard navigation.
